jobDescription:
Graduate/Post Graduate with 7+ years of overall experience, mandatory 5+ years in Release management &amp; ITSM modules with following criteria: Bachelor/ Master Degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Technology, or relevant field with 7-10 years of development experience 5+ years of Project management across lifecycle SDLC is mandatory (Formal experience of conducting TCQ, KPIs and project planning, scoping, execution) 5+ yrs ITSM/ITOM (all modules), deployment &amp; release management strong experience 5+ yrs of exp on Service-now/ Jira/ Rally/Version One or Agility tools Experience with automated release coordination tools (such as XL Release or Urban Code Release) Strong experience of ITIL processes (min foundation certification required) Agile (Scrum &amp; Kanban) hands-on experience working in cross-functional Agile teams from inception to release. Hands-on CI/CD and automation understanding 5-6 years of experience managing complex IT systems. Experience of managing maintenance &amp; operations activities 2+ yrs of Project management activities, complex stakeholder management, lean six sigma project implementation Strong experience as a functional and technical leader Proven experience of managing IT project combining cloud (AWS, GCP) and on-premises solutions, release &amp; deployment management Hands-on experience developing using Java Script &amp; relational databases. Knowledge on some of the following programming languages and concepts Java, XML, Python/Json, Javascript, Angular.js, but also on Linux system Knowledge on some of the following products/tools: Splunk, Ansible, Docker, Artifactory, Git Hub, Jenkins, Maven, Jira/Confluence, etc Dev Ops set-up knowledge: orientation, knowledge of continuous integration frameworks and some of the following products/tools: Docker, Nexus, Artifactory, Git Hub, Jenkins, Maven, Version One, Splunk, Elastic Search, Ansible, etc. Advanced level of English Accountabilities &amp;

RESPONSIBILITIES:
